@tradition storm-stories
// Storm stories by torchlight (FX26, 0.93.2; the user's pick of CS1's options, via lead 37, 2026-10-26). The ion storm's
// Saturday (Day 13 in a new game), 21:00-21:45, after the lantern supper: the junior common room, main lights off,
// torches. Matthias Oduya hosts (tap him to join); everyone tells the worst storm they've been in, torch under the chin,
// a little worse than the truth. Never on its own rhythm: the storm adds it to its Saturday (STORM_SAT_ON, the storm's
// dayDress), so a game without the storm (or with the switch off) never has it. Holt and Mensah are on duty then.
// CS1's words (plans/storm-stories-words.txt on claude/crew-stories-pitch c7e67663); the eight tellers' snippets are
// among the `here` lines; while it runs they're also said aloud in turn (section 18's stormStoriesFrame), with Oduya's
// close lines near the end (in the game, as the format has no place for them): "That's the last torch. Lights stay low. Sleep well, and let the storm do its job." and "Good
// stories. Mostly true. Off to bed, and leave your torch by the door."; his join lines are the join toast (join.lines).
k: 474
title: Storm stories by torchlight
when: year day 13 until day 1
at: 21:00-21:45
min: 20
// a place kept for you in the circle (RV18's S1: the room filled and you stood in the corridor)
spare: 1
where: 4 pool common-room
hold: 1
who: oduya always, holt never, mensah never, night-owl 70%, juniors 40%, everyone 25%
anim: oduya talk
host: oduya
from: oduya
invite: host=oduya odds=40% line="Storm stories tonight, after the supper. Bring a torch and your worst storm."

== mail
- Storm stories tomorrow night, {time}, the junior common room, after the lantern supper. Lights off, torches on. Bring the worst storm you've ever been in. You may exaggerate.

== ask
- Storm stories after the supper. Oduya says to bring a torch.
- Have you got a worst storm? Everyone's got a worst storm.
- Torchlight in the common room tonight. I'm telling the one about the roof.   #funny

== here
- And then the window just... went. Whoosh. Well. Creaked.   #funny
- Torch under your chin. No, higher. There. Terrifying.   #funny
- That's not the worst storm. That's weather.   #funny
- Shh, the lights. Oh. No, just a flicker. Carry on.
- I'd have hidden under the table. I did hide under the table.   #funny
- Tell it again, but bigger this time.
- Hailstones the size of eggs on the farm moon. We ate the hail. It was not eggs.   #funny
- Our station lost power for a whole night. We played cards by the light of the fish tank.
- A dust storm on Marra. Three days indoors. My brother learnt every song I hate.   #funny
- The ferry rocked so much the soup went sideways. All of it. Onto the captain.   #funny
- Wind took our washing line clean off. We found a sock in the next village.   #funny
- Lightning hit the radio mast. Every radio in town played the same song for a week.
- I slept through the worst storm in forty years. I'm still annoyed about it.   #funny
- Snowed in at Gran's with one book. I know that book by heart now.   #warm

== thanks
- In the dark common room, crewmates take turns telling the worst storm they've ever been in, torch under the chin. Each one a little worse than the truth.   #warm

== chatter
- Storm stories last night. Somebody's hail was the size of melons by the third telling.   #funny
- I didn't think I'd laugh on a storm night. Then the torch stories.   #warm
- Oduya told one too. Just one. It was the best one.
